  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating an aspiration level as the mean of outcomes (ignoring probabilities), computing differences between outcomes and this level, and then comparing the probabilities of positive differences. The individual did not mention any such calculation or reference to a mean or aspiration level. Instead, they focused on the favorable outcomes (2400 and 2500) and the perceived fairness of the chances, while dismissing the 1% risk. Although the individual did consider the probability of non-zero outcomes (implying a focus on positive outcomes), they did not evaluate the probability of outcomes exceeding a calculated aspiration level. The reasoning process described is more aligned with risk tolerance and outcome evaluation than with a formal comparison based on deviations from a mean. Therefore, while there is some superficial similarity (favoring outcomes above a threshold), the core mechanism of the decision reason—using a mean-based aspiration level and comparing probabilities of positive deviations—is absent from the verbal report. The individual did not use the specified reason.",
